vow 1 component logging_setup
# archvow vow of logging_setup - what it must be and do; archvow check holds the code to it.
# Read: archvow show logging_setup. Change: archvow specify logging_setup. Never edit by hand.
name logging_setup
type foundation
layer p0_common
module my_pipeline.p0_common.logging_setup
description "Configures logging once, for the entry point - the only place that configures it (ARCH059 - no basicConfig, handler or root level anywhere else); every module takes its own logger with logging.getLogger(__name__). Level from the config, one line per event on stderr - the cluster keeps it - with the run id and the run date, never a secret, a row or personal data; the tests put the logging back as it was after each test (a shared fixture of tests/conftest.py - later logs, Spark's too, must not write to a test's closed stream)."
uses []

